  "description": "The Chedi Andermatt is a hotel at Gotthardstrasse 4, CH-6490 Andermatt, in the Urseren Valley of the Swiss Alps. The village sits at 1,440 metres. The 2026 factsheet counts 120 rooms and suites. The telephone is +41 41 888 74 88 and reservations go to reservations@thechediandermatt.com. The map on the hotel site places the house at 46.6364826 north and 8.5941959 east.\n\nThe list runs from Alpine Deluxe Rooms and Furka View Deluxe Rooms through junior suites, deluxe suites and two-bedroom suites. Three signature suites close the list: the Gemsstock Suite at 115 square metres, the Oberalp three-bedroom suite at 189 square metres, and the Furka three-bedroom suite at 318 square metres, which has a private spa. Heated indoor and outdoor pools sit with the spa. The day spa covers 2,400 square metres, with saunas, steam baths and a fitness studio. Personal training and private yoga can be requested.\n\nThe Restaurant serves Asian and European cooking from four open kitchens, with 14 GaultMillau points and a five-metre glass cheese cellar. The Japanese holds three Michelin stars and 18 GaultMillau points, and has received the Michelin Young Chef Award. The Japanese at Gütsch holds one Michelin star and 17 GaultMillau points. The Cigar Library keeps 900 cigars from 15 countries. The Wine Library, the Bar and Living Room, the Lobby and the Courtyard complete the rooms for eating and drinking.\n\nBy car the hotel is 90 minutes from Zurich and 60 minutes from Lucerne. After the motorway exit at Goschenen, Andermatt is about 10 minutes further. Milan is about two hours, and Munich and Stuttgart about four. Zurich main station is less than two hours by train. Andermatt station, where the Glacier Express stops, is within walking distance. From Zurich Airport the drive is about 90 minutes, and from Milan airport about two hours. The factsheet lists hiking and skiing among the things to do in the valley.\n\nThe hotel suits a stay in the village, with the spa and the pools in the house and the station a walk away. Winter is the ski season and summer the season for paths. The 120 rooms and suites are the whole of the house, from an Alpine room to the Furka suite with its own spa.",
